# The pointer moves when a finger lifts.
#
# The panel reports a position change AFTER the pressure reaches 0, and before
# it reports the touch as up:
#
#   ABS_MT_PRESSURE   12 -> 9 -> 3 -> 0
#   ABS_MT_POSITION_X          -> 1943     <- at pressure 0
#   BTN_TOUCH         -> 0
#
# libinput still holds the contact at that point, thus it passes that last
# movement to the pointer. AttrPressureRange=<high>:<low> releases the contact
# below <low>, thus the move at pressure 0 is discarded.
#
# Measured on this panel with evtest, 16 press-and-lift cycles:
#   lightest touch peak  20      thus high=10 registers every touch
#   lift decay           12 9 3 0  thus low=6 releases between the 9 and the 3
# CAUTION: These are raw device units for THIS panel. They mean nothing on
# another touchpad. Measure again; do not copy.
# NOTE: libinput ships a quirk for this panel already, in
# 30-vendor-goodix.quirks: it sets AttrInputProp=+INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD, thus
# the pad is a haptic pressure pad and a click is a pressure reading. This file
# adds a pressure range to that entry; it does not replace it.
# CAUTION: libinput reads the quirks files once, when the compositor makes its
# libinput context. A change here needs a new session. `udevadm trigger` is not
# enough; that re-adds the device but keeps the parsed quirks.
[Goodix GXTP5420 Touchpad 27C6:0F95 pressure range]
MatchBus=i2c
MatchVendor=0x27C6
MatchProduct=0x0F95
MatchUdevType=touchpad
AttrPressureRange=10:6
